WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.836
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:01.106 --> 00:03.442
[♪ theme song playing]

3
00:03.525 --> 00:04.651
PARK MINJAE'S LIST

4
00:04.735 --> 00:06.028
START DATING...

5
00:36.725 --> 00:41.063
BETWEEN STEPS

6
00:41.688 --> 00:43.940
CHARACTERS, PLACES, ORGANIZATIONS, AND EVENTS IN THIS DRAMA ARE FICTITIOUS

7
00:44.024 --> 00:45.651
THIS DRAMA CONTAINS SENSITIVE CONTENT

8
00:46.777 --> 00:48.987
EPISODE 9

9
01:05.712 --> 01:07.714
[vacuum whirring]

10
01:19.184 --> 01:21.186
[vacuum whirring stops]

11
02:20.871 --> 02:22.873
[♪ dramatic Italian ballad playing, Gigliola Cinquetti "Non Ho L'Età"]

12
04:24.160 --> 04:26.162
[♪ dramatic Italian ballad continues playing]

13
04:56.443 --> 04:57.611
[door opens]

14
04:58.820 --> 04:59.821
[door closes]

15
05:01.072 --> 05:03.074
[tires screeching]

16
05:31.686 --> 05:33.688
[♪ music swells]

17
05:34.773 --> 05:36.566
-[♪ music stops] -[Youjin gasps]

18
05:36.650 --> 05:38.610
I'VE BEEN DYING TO SEE YOU!

19
05:38.693 --> 05:40.695
WELCOME

20
05:47.077 --> 05:48.286
[Youjin chuckles softly]

21
05:49.204 --> 05:51.206
You didn't have to come all this way.

22
05:51.289 --> 05:53.416
You're the guest of honor. Of course, I should.

23
05:53.500 --> 05:54.501
Let me take that.

24
05:54.584 --> 05:56.878
Leave it. I can get it.

25
05:56.962 --> 05:58.797
-I should take it. -It's okay.

26
05:59.881 --> 06:02.300
I could've taken a cab. Why did you come all this way?

27
06:02.384 --> 06:03.927
Got nothing better to do?

28
06:04.010 --> 06:06.137
[sighs] I've got plenty to do, but I came anyway.

29
06:06.221 --> 06:08.390
Because I missed you so much.

30
06:09.224 --> 06:10.892
Well, I didn't get you any gifts.

31
06:11.977 --> 06:12.978
Okay.

32
06:14.312 --> 06:15.313
Let's get a taxi.

33
06:15.397 --> 06:17.232
[exclaims softly] But I drove here.

34
06:19.359 --> 06:20.360
Did you buy a car?

35
06:21.528 --> 06:22.529
No.

36
06:23.321 --> 06:24.322
Huh?

37
06:35.041 --> 06:36.042
[Youjin] Hop in.

38
06:39.546 --> 06:41.548
Hey, why would you bring this out here?

39
06:42.632 --> 06:45.385
[Youjin] You have a lot of luggage, and I figured you'd be tired.

40
06:45.468 --> 06:46.720
And taxis are expensive.

41
06:48.638 --> 06:51.099
My car is more expensive than a taxi. Move.

42
06:52.892 --> 06:54.060
[Youjin] I'm a good driver.

43
06:54.144 --> 06:55.979
-I can get you home nice and comfortable. -[Jihoon grunts]

44
06:56.563 --> 06:59.816
Hey, all I asked you to do was water the plants

45
06:59.899 --> 07:01.234
and look after my place.

46
07:02.736 --> 07:04.863
You've been driving my car around, haven't you?

47
07:04.946 --> 07:05.947
No.

48
07:06.698 --> 07:09.993
-What do you take me for? -[Jihoon grunting]

49
07:12.454 --> 07:13.496
-Give me that. -Huh?

50
07:14.330 --> 07:15.540
I can drive.

51
07:17.667 --> 07:18.668
[Jihoon] Just get in.

52
07:20.587 --> 07:21.588
[scoffs]

53
07:33.850 --> 07:36.394
-[Youjin] Huh? -[Jihoon exclaims softly, scoffs]

54
07:37.312 --> 07:38.313
[Jihoon snickers]

55
07:41.983 --> 07:43.109
Put your seatbelt on.

56
07:43.193 --> 07:44.194
[Youjin] Okay.

57
07:45.111 --> 07:46.529
You've had a long flight,

58
07:47.447 --> 07:49.199
and you must be jet-lagged.

59
07:49.282 --> 07:50.617
Seriously, I can drive.

60
07:50.700 --> 07:51.951
Speak for yourself.

61
07:52.035 --> 07:55.872
You must be exhausted from coursework, exams, and your thesis.

62
07:55.955 --> 07:58.458
[inhales] So why'd you come all the way out here?

63
07:58.541 --> 07:59.626
In my car, no less?

64
08:02.754 --> 08:03.755
Huh?

65
08:05.924 --> 08:08.635
Well... You know, Professor,

66
08:08.718 --> 08:11.137
you've got a lot of connections, right?

67
08:12.305 --> 08:13.473
[Jihoon] I do. And?

68
08:14.474 --> 08:18.686
Do you know a Russian mathematician, Aleksandr Lyapunov?

69
08:19.270 --> 08:20.939
I hear he's super famous.

70
08:21.022 --> 08:22.315
I do.

71
08:22.398 --> 08:25.485
We're close. He died in 1918.

72
08:25.568 --> 08:27.237
[gasps] Yeah, him.

73
08:27.320 --> 08:28.321
-[Jihoon] Yeah? -Yeah.

74
08:28.822 --> 08:30.615
I knew you'd know him.

75
08:31.324 --> 08:32.492
[chuckles]

76
08:34.327 --> 08:35.495
[sighs]

77
08:36.371 --> 08:37.372
[♪ somber music playing]

78
08:37.455 --> 08:42.460
KIM JISEOK AND LEE JIHYE JANUARY 27, 2027, 2:00 PM

79
08:42.544 --> 08:43.545
PLEASE JOIN US

80
08:43.628 --> 08:45.964
AT LAST, WE'VE FOUND THE ONE TO SHARE OUR LIVES WITH

81
08:47.507 --> 08:49.509
FOR YOUR KIND WISHES BRIDE LEE JIHYE

82
08:51.845 --> 08:52.929
ACCOUNT NUMBER COPIED

83
08:56.850 --> 08:58.518
CHECKING ACCOUNT 42,700 WON

84
08:59.936 --> 09:03.064
-[♪ somber music turns comical] -[cellphone thuds]

85
09:06.526 --> 09:08.528
[♪ music stops]

86
09:10.280 --> 09:13.283
All solutions of the dynamical system

87
09:13.366 --> 09:18.121
that start near a Lyapunov-stable equilibrium point stay near it forever.

88
09:19.622 --> 09:21.166
[♪ comical music resumes playing]

89
09:21.249 --> 09:22.375
Forever.

90
09:26.421 --> 09:29.591
The above definition can be understood as follows.

91
09:29.674 --> 09:33.928
Solutions that start sufficiently close to a Lyapunov-stable equilibrium

92
09:34.012 --> 09:37.432
remain sufficiently close to the equilibrium forever,

93
09:38.516 --> 09:41.227
with the allowable deviation being arbitrarily small.

94
09:43.897 --> 09:47.650
Solutions that start sufficiently close to an asymptotically stable equilibrium

95
09:47.734 --> 09:49.736
not only stay close to it,

96
09:49.819 --> 09:52.906
but also eventually converge to the equilibrium.

97
09:56.576 --> 10:00.455
Solutions that start sufficiently close to an exponentially stable equilibrium

98
10:00.538 --> 10:04.083
eventually converge exponentially,

99
10:04.167 --> 10:07.545
at least as fast as a particular known rate.

100
10:09.589 --> 10:10.632
[Jihoon sighs]

101
10:12.133 --> 10:13.885
Come to think of it, I'm kind of hurt.

102
10:15.261 --> 10:19.140
You went all the way to the States and seriously didn't get me anything?

103
10:20.266 --> 10:22.268
[♪ music stops]

104
10:23.353 --> 10:26.481
It's Christmas soon. You could've picked up a little something.

105
10:28.483 --> 10:30.485
Not even some chocolate or something?

106
10:30.568 --> 10:32.153
Do you think I went there for fun?

107
10:32.237 --> 10:34.864
I was attending a conference. I didn't have time for that.

108
10:35.907 --> 10:38.952
I mean, they sell chocolate at the airport duty-free stores.

109
10:40.620 --> 10:43.081
It's not like I want to eat American chocolate.

110
10:43.790 --> 10:46.292
It's the thought that counts, you know?

111
10:53.174 --> 10:54.842
[exclaims] What's that?

112
10:55.343 --> 10:56.928
Are you giving me money instead?

113
10:58.471 --> 10:59.597
[Jihoon] Here. Your gift.

114
11:02.350 --> 11:03.351
What's this?

115
11:15.280 --> 11:17.031
I met Park Minjae there.

116
11:20.034 --> 11:22.370
I thought he was in Canada, but he's in the US.

117
11:24.330 --> 11:26.833
I asked him if he'd been in Canada, and he said no.

118
11:27.458 --> 11:29.085
He said he went back to the States.

119
11:30.837 --> 11:33.006
Turns out he's working on some project with MIT.

120
11:34.215 --> 11:35.216
Did you know?

121
11:37.844 --> 11:40.430
Other than his hairstyle, he looked pretty much the same.

122
11:41.014 --> 11:42.682
He seemed to be doing well.

123
11:46.102 --> 11:47.562
I said you were doing well, too.

124
11:47.645 --> 11:50.398
That you're eating well, attending school, and studying hard.

125
11:52.734 --> 11:55.153
That's his new number, so give him a call if you want.

126
11:58.156 --> 11:59.198
[scoffs softly]

127
12:00.033 --> 12:01.534
What would I even say?

128
12:02.744 --> 12:04.245
There's nothing to talk about.

129
12:05.705 --> 12:07.040
[sighs]

130
12:07.123 --> 12:09.667
It's not like I'm going to cry and curse him out.

131
12:13.046 --> 12:17.091
Well, breakups are hard and painful for everyone.

132
12:17.175 --> 12:19.802
Your relationship wasn't anything special.

133
12:19.886 --> 12:23.139
That's what relationships are like. They can end just like that.

134
12:26.184 --> 12:27.185
[sighs]

135
12:27.268 --> 12:28.519
You know what, Professor?

136
12:29.520 --> 12:31.397
You talk too much.

137
12:31.481 --> 12:33.107
Because I know a lot.

138
12:33.941 --> 12:35.401
There's nothing I don't know.

139
12:38.404 --> 12:41.824
Have you never liked a woman before?

140
12:41.908 --> 12:42.909
Well...

141
12:44.202 --> 12:47.163
I've just never been dumped by a woman I liked.

142
12:48.331 --> 12:49.332
[Youjin scoffs]

143
12:50.333 --> 12:52.418
I guess you never get hurt or anything.

144
12:52.502 --> 12:55.254
No. I'm a deep, grounded person.

145
12:56.214 --> 12:57.256
[sighs]

146
12:59.967 --> 13:01.052
What?

147
13:01.761 --> 13:03.763
[paper rustling]

148
13:07.225 --> 13:08.226
Hey.

149
13:11.104 --> 13:13.940
Hey, no littering. You should put it in a trash can.

150
13:15.566 --> 13:17.860
I pray that the woman he likes brutally dumps him

151
13:17.944 --> 13:19.779
and leaves him in tears.

152
13:22.156 --> 13:24.784
You're praying that happens to Park Minjae, not me, right?

153
13:26.411 --> 13:28.579
No. To both of you.

154
13:32.917 --> 13:34.919
[♪ gentle music playing]

155
14:59.045 --> 15:00.379
[sighs heavily]

156
15:00.463 --> 15:02.465
[♪ music fades]

157
15:13.684 --> 15:14.685
[sighs]

158
15:16.145 --> 15:17.396
[door closes]

159
15:17.480 --> 15:20.233
[Miyoung] Oh... Youjin is home, so lock the doors.

160
15:23.361 --> 15:25.279
[Yongseok] Be gentle. I'm scared.

161
15:25.363 --> 15:28.157
[Miyoung] Okay, stay still. I'm scared too. [gasps]

162
15:28.241 --> 15:29.700
[woman screaming on TV]

163
15:31.494 --> 15:32.495
What's up?

164
15:34.121 --> 15:35.539
[Youseong] Can I have 100,000 won?

165
15:35.623 --> 15:36.874
I don't have it.

166
15:37.458 --> 15:39.210
You're not even going to ask why?

167
15:40.127 --> 15:42.463
You always say no even without asking. Always.

168
15:44.632 --> 15:45.925
What do you need it for?

169
15:46.801 --> 15:48.052
[Youseong] I can't tell you.

170
15:48.970 --> 15:50.137
[mouthing] Jeez.

171
15:50.972 --> 15:53.432
[Youseong] Come on, can't you just give me 100,000 won?

172
15:53.516 --> 15:55.893
There's a reason I need it.

173
15:56.978 --> 15:58.938
-Mom, just give me my allowance early. -Hey!

174
15:59.021 --> 16:01.482
Jeez. You're not getting it early.

175
16:01.565 --> 16:03.109
-[Youseong] Dad. -Hey!

176
16:03.651 --> 16:06.654
Dude, the boss says no.

177
16:07.238 --> 16:08.239
Then what about me?

178
16:08.864 --> 16:10.533
What am I? Huh?

179
16:11.158 --> 16:14.078
I'm the eldest son and the heir to the auto repair shop.

180
16:14.161 --> 16:15.871
I'll inherit the whole thing someday.

181
16:15.955 --> 16:18.040
You can't even do that much for your own heir?

182
16:18.124 --> 16:19.917
Heir, my foot.

183
16:20.835 --> 16:23.504
Honey, what do you think he's saying?

184
16:24.255 --> 16:26.549
I don't know. I can't hear well right now.

185
16:27.675 --> 16:28.676
[Youseong] Then, Mom...

186
16:28.759 --> 16:29.760
[Miyoung, softly] Yeah.

187
16:29.844 --> 16:31.220
[Youseong] If you give me 100,000 won,

188
16:31.887 --> 16:33.639
I'll give you this.

189
16:34.307 --> 16:35.308
What is it?

190
16:36.100 --> 16:37.101
[Youseong] I don't know.

191
16:37.184 --> 16:38.769
[♪ comical music playing]

192
16:38.853 --> 16:40.104
You're drunk, aren't you?

193
16:42.523 --> 16:43.858
Give me a break. Jeez.

194
16:50.531 --> 16:52.199
[gulps, sighs in relief]

195
16:59.874 --> 17:00.875
[sighs]

196
17:11.385 --> 17:14.972
NO RESULTS FOUND MATCHING +1 (617) 555-0754

197
17:15.056 --> 17:18.059
[keyboard clacking]

198
17:18.142 --> 17:19.894
+1 (617) SERVES BOSTON, MASSACHUSETTS...

199
17:19.977 --> 17:22.063
[Youseong] Massachusetts in the US?

200
17:22.146 --> 17:23.689
[slurring] Messasuses?

201
17:26.067 --> 17:28.986
[groans] This is why I hate English.

202
17:29.987 --> 17:31.572
The pronunciation is just too hard.

203
17:32.448 --> 17:33.449
[sighs]

204
17:37.495 --> 17:39.497
[♪ comical music continues playing]

205
17:51.342 --> 17:52.343
[line connects]

206
17:52.885 --> 17:54.470
-[line ringing] -[sighs softly]

207
18:01.227 --> 18:02.228
[exhales]

208
18:02.937 --> 18:03.938
[groans]

209
18:07.817 --> 18:08.818
[tuts]

210
18:09.276 --> 18:10.277
[sighs heavily]

211
18:11.946 --> 18:14.865
Not answering. Not answering.

212
18:16.200 --> 18:17.785
-[sighs] -[man in English] Hello?

213
18:19.078 --> 18:20.079
[in Korean] Hello?

214
18:20.705 --> 18:21.956
[in Korean] Yes, hello?

215
18:22.039 --> 18:23.249
[♪ music stops]

216
18:23.332 --> 18:24.333
Uh...

217
18:24.417 --> 18:26.627
Are you in Massachusetts, by any chance?

218
18:26.711 --> 18:27.712
[man] Pardon?

219
18:28.379 --> 18:29.380
Who are you?

220
18:30.005 --> 18:33.050
I said, are you in Massachusetts?

221
18:35.052 --> 18:38.514
You're in the United... I mean, America, right?

222
18:38.597 --> 18:40.015
[man] Yes, I am. Who are you?

223
18:40.099 --> 18:41.100
[in English] Hello?

224
18:42.101 --> 18:44.019
[man in English] Hello? Hello?

225
18:45.271 --> 18:46.272
[in English] Hello?

226
18:47.481 --> 18:48.482
[man in Korean] What?

227
18:49.442 --> 18:52.236
I think you may have the wrong number.

228
18:52.319 --> 18:54.113
Who were you trying to call?

229
18:54.196 --> 18:55.197
[in Korean] What?

230
18:56.115 --> 18:58.784
I'm Lim Youseong.

231
18:59.410 --> 19:00.536
I'm Korean.

232
19:02.955 --> 19:04.039
Who are you?

233
19:48.709 --> 19:50.711
[♪ mysterious music playing]

234
20:16.570 --> 20:17.571
A ghost?

235
20:29.124 --> 20:31.126
[♪ music fades]

236
20:31.210 --> 20:32.211
Ah...

237
20:37.758 --> 20:39.760
[♪ gentle music playing]

238
21:39.695 --> 21:41.697
[♪ music fades]

239
21:52.666 --> 21:54.668
[♪ gentle music resumes playing]

240
23:23.757 --> 23:25.759
-[♪ music fades] -[jewelry box snaps shut]

241
23:36.353 --> 23:37.354
[Yongseok sighs]

242
23:39.481 --> 23:40.649
[Youseong groans]

243
23:41.859 --> 23:44.319
[exclaims] It's bean sprout soup.

244
23:44.403 --> 23:47.614
[Miyoung] It's all for our heir, our eldest son.

245
23:47.698 --> 23:49.867
We can't have him suffering from a hangover.

246
23:51.118 --> 23:52.286
[Youseong grunts]

247
23:52.369 --> 23:53.370
[Yongseok] Hey, sweetie. Come, have a seat.

248
23:53.454 --> 23:54.455
[Youjin] Okay.

249
23:54.538 --> 23:56.623
Mom made some refreshing bean sprout soup.

250
23:56.707 --> 23:59.001
[Youjin] I'm running late, so I'll have to skip breakfast.

251
23:59.084 --> 24:00.294
[Miyoung] Come on, how long does it take

252
24:00.377 --> 24:02.504
-to eat breakfast? Hmm? -[Youjin] Mmm-mmm.

253
24:02.588 --> 24:04.798
What's the point of working if you don't eat?

254
24:04.882 --> 24:07.134
You're practically skin and bones.

255
24:07.718 --> 24:09.553
Yeah, have some breakfast before you go.

256
24:09.636 --> 24:11.555
We'll ask Youseong to give you a ride.

257
24:11.638 --> 24:13.390
Yeah, that would work.

258
24:13.474 --> 24:16.518
Youseong's giving you a ride today. Eat before you go.

259
24:16.602 --> 24:18.270
-I am? -[Miyoung] Yeah.

260
24:18.353 --> 24:21.857
Or how about I take Dad's car? I can drive.

261
24:21.940 --> 24:23.108
Come on, no.

262
24:23.192 --> 24:25.360
You still need more practice.

263
24:25.444 --> 24:27.196
Youseong can give you a ride.

264
24:27.279 --> 24:28.280
[Miyoung] Yeah, just do that.

265
24:28.363 --> 24:30.199
-Don't worry. Just sit down and eat. -[Miyoung] Yeah.

266
24:30.282 --> 24:31.366
[Youseong groans]

267
24:32.826 --> 24:34.244
[Miyoung] Come on, let's eat.

268
24:36.246 --> 24:37.247
Let's eat.

269
24:37.331 --> 24:38.332
Come on.

270
24:38.415 --> 24:40.417
-I'll give you a ride. -[Miyoung] Good. Sit here.

271
24:41.251 --> 24:42.252
Oh, man.

272
25:14.660 --> 25:16.245
-Thanks. [in English] Thank you. -[seatbelt unlocks]

273
25:16.328 --> 25:17.830
[in Korean] Hey.

274
25:17.913 --> 25:19.414
Are you going to keep that in?

275
25:19.498 --> 25:20.499
[Youjin] Oh...

276
25:25.546 --> 25:26.588
Bye now.

277
25:26.672 --> 25:27.673
Youjin.

278
25:28.423 --> 25:29.633
You see,

279
25:30.384 --> 25:34.054
you're my one and only little sister,

280
25:34.805 --> 25:38.851
and I really, truly care about you so much.

281
25:38.934 --> 25:39.935
What?

282
25:40.519 --> 25:44.815
[smacks lips] I mean, sometimes I get in your business,

283
25:44.898 --> 25:50.571
nag you, or even get pretty scary and yell at you, right?

284
25:50.654 --> 25:52.030
[smacks lips]

285
25:52.114 --> 25:56.702
But it's all because I care about you, Youjin. Okay?

286
25:56.785 --> 25:58.579
I just want what's best for you.

287
25:59.746 --> 26:03.208
I hope you understand where your big brother is coming from.

288
26:04.168 --> 26:05.252
It's not scary.

289
26:06.253 --> 26:07.254
[Youseong] What?

290
26:08.046 --> 26:09.298
It's not scary.

291
26:09.923 --> 26:11.008
It's annoying.

292
26:14.428 --> 26:15.429
Fine.

293
26:15.929 --> 26:17.222
Get out. Go.

294
26:18.390 --> 26:20.475
[smacks lips, sighs]

295
26:26.440 --> 26:27.441
[mumbles] What the hell?

296
26:42.706 --> 26:44.708
[♪ quirky music playing]

297
26:49.588 --> 26:51.089
CALLING +1 617-555-0754

298
26:51.173 --> 26:52.549
[line ringing]

299
26:55.844 --> 26:56.845
[sighs softly]

300
27:00.015 --> 27:02.184
[automation in English] The person you are calling is not answering...

301
27:03.227 --> 27:05.187
-[line disconnects] -[sighs]

302
27:05.270 --> 27:09.399
Once that brat finds out, she's going to freak out totally.

303
27:17.449 --> 27:18.450
[line connects]

304
27:18.533 --> 27:19.534
[line ringing]

305
27:25.082 --> 27:26.583
Hey, Subin.

306
27:26.667 --> 27:28.210
Yeah, it's me, Youseong.

307
27:30.212 --> 27:32.589
Well, I happened to be at your campus right now.

308
27:32.673 --> 27:33.799
Do you have a minute?

309
27:36.134 --> 27:38.804
There's something I wanted to ask you about Youjin.

310
27:39.304 --> 27:40.347
Yeah.

311
27:40.430 --> 27:42.808
No, don't tell Youjin about this.

312
27:44.059 --> 27:45.227
Yeah.

313
27:45.310 --> 27:46.520
Okay, got it.

314
27:48.230 --> 27:50.232
-[♪ music fades] -[mouse clicking]

315
27:55.112 --> 27:57.364
-[door opens] -[♪ pensive music playing]

316
27:58.699 --> 28:01.660
[Taeho sighing] All right. Good morning, everyone.

317
28:01.743 --> 28:03.078
Good morning.

318
28:03.161 --> 28:04.329
[Taeho] Mmm-hmm.

319
28:05.539 --> 28:06.957
[Taeho hums]

320
28:12.087 --> 28:13.088
All right.

321
28:15.841 --> 28:16.842
[sighs]

322
28:20.595 --> 28:22.014
[bell rings, thuds]

323
28:22.097 --> 28:23.390
Let's start the meeting.

324
28:27.310 --> 28:30.480
Finals are over, so things have settled down.

325
28:31.398 --> 28:34.484
We've got a lab meeting next week, right? Whose turn is it?

326
28:35.485 --> 28:36.903
[hesitates] My turn.

327
28:38.030 --> 28:39.072
Are you ready?

328
28:39.156 --> 28:41.241
Yeah, well...

329
28:41.324 --> 28:42.325
[Taeho sighs]

330
28:42.409 --> 28:44.578
The other labs will be there, too.

331
28:44.661 --> 28:46.121
Our reputation is on the line.

332
28:46.788 --> 28:49.541
So you'd better be prepared. Don't embarrass us.

333
28:50.417 --> 28:51.418
[softly] Okay.

334
28:51.501 --> 28:54.046
[Hangyeol] But it seemed like it was getting pushed back a week.

335
28:54.129 --> 28:55.130
[Taeho] Why?

336
28:55.213 --> 28:59.468
[Sejin] The Thomas and Dalmatian labs wanted to reschedule,

337
28:59.551 --> 29:01.595
since Christmas is next week and all.

338
29:01.678 --> 29:02.679
[Taeho] Really?

339
29:04.139 --> 29:06.641
[Sejin sighing] Apparently, the Thomas guys are going

340
29:06.725 --> 29:08.977
on a group blind date with the piano majors.

341
29:09.061 --> 29:10.270
[Taeho and Hangyeol scoff]

342
29:10.353 --> 29:13.732
I think there's almost 100% chance that they'll reschedule.

343
29:13.815 --> 29:16.068
-[Taeho sighs heavily] -Jeez, those crazy bastards...

344
29:16.151 --> 29:19.696
[chuckling] Wow, sounds like things are just as messed up over there.

345
29:20.363 --> 29:21.615
[laughs, sighs]

346
29:22.324 --> 29:26.828
What's with the obsession with these blind dates? [laughs]

347
29:26.912 --> 29:29.331
And yet, Korea has the lowest birth rate in the world.

348
29:29.414 --> 29:30.999
-Exactly. -[Taeho] Right?

349
29:31.083 --> 29:33.043
It's not like we don't want to go on them.

350
29:33.126 --> 29:34.753
[Hangyeol sighs]

351
29:34.836 --> 29:38.215
Those damn punks don't know Christmas is for families.

352
29:38.965 --> 29:39.966
You'll see.

353
29:40.801 --> 29:45.722
There's going to be a bloodbath next semester.

354
29:46.556 --> 29:47.557
[Chansoo] Hmm.

355
29:48.767 --> 29:52.562
I guess we can come back to the lab meeting date next time, then.

356
29:53.563 --> 29:55.649
Youjin, have you decided on your thesis topic?

357
29:56.858 --> 29:59.903
No. I mean, I'm still thinking.

358
30:00.529 --> 30:03.490
I'm debating between optimal design and control algorithms,

359
30:03.573 --> 30:06.076
-but I haven't decided yet. -[knocks on table]

360
30:06.159 --> 30:08.829
[Taeho] You've got to hurry, okay?

361
30:08.912 --> 30:11.248
What's taking you so long, Youjin?

362
30:11.873 --> 30:12.874
Okay.

363
30:14.126 --> 30:15.627
[sighs] And you, Sejin?

364
30:15.710 --> 30:17.754
Yes, I've decided.

365
30:19.047 --> 30:21.341
You did? What did you pick?

366
30:21.424 --> 30:22.717
[Sejin inhales]

367
30:22.801 --> 30:24.928
I'm not going to tell you.

368
30:38.900 --> 30:39.901
[line connects]

369
30:39.985 --> 30:41.236
[line ringing]

370
30:52.956 --> 30:54.958
[♪ pensive music builds]

371
31:06.845 --> 31:08.847
[♪ exhilarating music playing]

372
31:34.664 --> 31:35.665
[door opens]

373
31:38.126 --> 31:39.127
[door closes]

374
31:49.304 --> 31:51.306
[♪ music fades]

375
31:51.389 --> 31:52.390
[Jihoon] Hey.

376
31:56.603 --> 32:00.232
If you manage to prove this, you have to put my name in the paper.

377
32:03.610 --> 32:05.153
Will you not?

378
32:05.237 --> 32:06.363
I will.

379
32:07.364 --> 32:08.990
[Youjin] And give me the prize money, too?

380
32:09.074 --> 32:11.534
Not all of it, just some. A little bit?

381
32:12.285 --> 32:15.956
Why are you so obsessed with money? It's the honor that matters.

382
32:16.539 --> 32:17.540
So you won't?

383
32:18.166 --> 32:20.543
There's no prize money. It's just for the honor.

384
32:21.127 --> 32:22.128
[Youjin] Hmm.

385
32:22.212 --> 32:24.047
There's no prize money for this one.

386
32:27.509 --> 32:30.929
[Jihoon] But I did bring you something back from the seminar.

387
32:31.012 --> 32:32.389
It's not chocolate, though.

388
32:33.098 --> 32:34.266
It's kind of expensive.

389
32:35.433 --> 32:37.227
You really got me a gift?

390
32:37.310 --> 32:38.645
Got any plans next Friday?

391
32:39.145 --> 32:41.273
I'll take you to dinner and give you your gift.

392
32:41.856 --> 32:43.650
Okay. Friday works for me, too.

393
32:44.609 --> 32:46.111
[muttering] 23, 25...

394
32:46.861 --> 32:49.447
[exclaims] Isn't it Christmas that day?

395
32:50.824 --> 32:52.158
Is it?

396
32:53.743 --> 32:56.371
Forget it. Traffic will be terrible, it'll be packed.

397
32:56.454 --> 32:57.706
No, it's too troublesome.

398
32:57.789 --> 32:58.790
[clicks tongue]

399
32:59.624 --> 33:00.625
[sighs]

400
33:02.335 --> 33:04.170
[Jihoon] But I don't have time on any other day.

401
33:07.215 --> 33:08.508
What do we do?

402
33:08.591 --> 33:11.219
Then, can we just do Friday?

403
33:12.137 --> 33:15.765
Places like Gangnam, Hongdae, and Seongsu will be packed,

404
33:15.849 --> 33:18.310
but I think it'll be okay around campus.

405
33:18.393 --> 33:19.519
You think?

406
33:19.602 --> 33:20.603
[Youjin] Yeah.

407
33:22.731 --> 33:23.732
Well, then...

408
33:24.733 --> 33:25.734
I guess why not?

409
33:26.359 --> 33:27.360
[chuckles softly]

410
33:29.738 --> 33:32.866
Is there anything you want for Christmas?

411
33:32.949 --> 33:34.242
There isn't.

412
33:34.326 --> 33:36.786
Come on, tell me. This is a rare opportunity.

413
33:37.495 --> 33:39.080
Just tell me what you want.

414
33:44.627 --> 33:45.628
Then, you.

415
33:46.796 --> 33:48.965
[♪ pensive music playing]

416
33:52.302 --> 33:54.804
I mean, just having a meal with you is enough.

417
33:54.888 --> 33:56.681
I don't need any gifts.

418
33:57.223 --> 33:58.224
[Youjin] Hmm.

419
33:58.683 --> 34:00.602
So I really don't have to get you anything?

420
34:01.311 --> 34:02.687
Because I really won't.

421
34:03.313 --> 34:04.397
[Jihoon] Don't bother. [sighs]

422
34:04.481 --> 34:06.900
Knowing your taste, it will end up in the trash anyway.

423
34:07.567 --> 34:09.069
It's environmental pollution.

424
34:09.152 --> 34:11.446
We have to pay to throw stuff away in this country.

425
34:11.946 --> 34:14.032
[♪ pensive music turns comical]

426
34:14.115 --> 34:18.078
[sighs] I bet you wouldn't say that to me if we were in the US.

427
34:20.497 --> 34:21.498
What?

428
34:21.581 --> 34:23.792
I heard they sell guns at supermarkets in the US.

429
34:26.378 --> 34:29.381
I hope my gift is a gun.

430
34:29.464 --> 34:30.465
[Jihoon] Okay.

431
34:32.092 --> 34:33.093
It's not a gun.

432
34:36.429 --> 34:37.430
Now, go.

433
34:38.932 --> 34:39.933
[Youjin scoffs]

434
34:42.143 --> 34:43.144
[tuts]

435
34:44.521 --> 34:48.316
PROFESSOR LEE JIHOON'S OFFICE

436
34:48.983 --> 34:49.984
[mumbles] I swear to God...

437
34:54.280 --> 34:55.281
[exclaims softly]

438
34:56.324 --> 34:57.659
What did I come here for?

439
35:05.375 --> 35:07.377
[keyboard clacking]

440
35:09.879 --> 35:11.089
[sighs]

441
35:11.172 --> 35:13.925
I'm going to the library for a bit...

442
35:17.470 --> 35:18.471
[sighs. heavily]

443
35:34.988 --> 35:36.698
My goodness.

444
35:37.365 --> 35:39.367
Things are pretty messed up around here.

445
35:40.118 --> 35:42.412
[Taeho] Seriously, those assholes have lost their minds

446
35:42.495 --> 35:46.207
and are pushing back the lab meeting for some stupid group blind date.

447
35:46.291 --> 35:50.837
Those damn robot train nerds think our bipedal humanoid is a fucking joke.

448
35:51.629 --> 35:55.258
That's why you've got to get back here and clean house.

449
35:55.341 --> 35:57.761
We need a full-on bloodbath, Minjae.

450
35:58.344 --> 36:02.557
[Minjae laughing] What do you mean, a bloodbath? Don't be crazy.

451
36:04.058 --> 36:06.644
Hey, so, what about the Dalmatian guys?

452
36:09.063 --> 36:10.064
Yeah.

453
36:10.940 --> 36:11.941
Oh, really?

454
36:12.984 --> 36:14.903
Well, that's the right thing to do.

455
36:15.904 --> 36:20.533
Those guys are actually really generous. [laughing]

456
36:20.617 --> 36:21.743
[Taeho] Come on, Minjae.

457
36:21.826 --> 36:25.330
This isn't something you can just laugh off, okay?

458
36:25.914 --> 36:28.416
I'm telling you, you need to get back here, Minjae.

459
36:28.500 --> 36:30.168
When are you coming back, anyway?

460
36:30.960 --> 36:32.962
Yeah, but when? Hmm?

461
36:33.046 --> 36:34.339
Mmm.

462
36:34.422 --> 36:36.758
Really? [chuckles]

463
36:36.841 --> 36:38.676
Yeah, of course. I'll keep it to myself.

464
36:38.760 --> 36:40.553
None of the other guys will know. Yeah.

465
36:41.137 --> 36:44.140
Got it. But, Minjae, you really have to be here that day, okay?

466
36:44.224 --> 36:46.059
Okay, enough already.

467
36:47.352 --> 36:49.896
Just stop. [chuckling] I said I got it, you weirdo.

468
36:51.356 --> 36:52.482
All right.

469
36:52.565 --> 36:55.860
I'll call you back. Bye.

470
37:01.950 --> 37:03.159
[grunts]

471
37:05.954 --> 37:08.373
Mom, just leave it. I can take care of it later.

472
37:08.456 --> 37:09.749
[Eunjoo] It's okay. I'm done.

473
37:09.833 --> 37:11.626
[Minjae] No, let me... Gosh.

474
37:11.709 --> 37:14.629
-You want this up there? -[Eunjoo] Yeah. [laughs]

475
37:14.712 --> 37:19.092
Goodness. It's so nice having someone tall around.

476
37:19.175 --> 37:21.052
[Minjae] Now, leave it. I'll deal with them later.

477
37:21.135 --> 37:22.178
-[Eunjoo] Okay. -[Minjae] Come on.

478
37:22.762 --> 37:24.806
-Can I have a glass of water? -[Minjae] Sure.

479
37:35.483 --> 37:36.484
[Eunjoo sighs]

480
37:38.945 --> 37:42.115
My glasses... Where did I put the glasses?

481
37:42.198 --> 37:44.284
Don't bother. I can just drink it like that.

482
37:44.367 --> 37:45.577
-Yeah? -[Eunjoo] Yeah.

483
37:46.411 --> 37:47.412
[Minjae snickers]

484
37:48.454 --> 37:50.999
-I should get a new glass. -[Eunjoo chuckles]

485
37:52.125 --> 37:53.126
Yeah.

486
37:53.751 --> 37:54.878
[Minjae sighs]

487
37:54.961 --> 37:57.088
[Eunjoo] There were so many little things to unpack.

488
37:57.171 --> 37:58.631
And so much dust.

489
37:59.507 --> 38:02.510
If I'd known it would be this much work, I would've hired someone.

490
38:02.594 --> 38:04.178
[Minjae] No, it's okay. Later...

491
38:04.262 --> 38:06.723
I'll take my time unpacking everything later.

492
38:11.769 --> 38:15.398
[Eunjoo] You didn't forget what you promised me, right?

493
38:18.151 --> 38:19.485
No drinking.

494
38:20.820 --> 38:23.865
No wine or beer, nothing.

495
38:25.450 --> 38:26.451
[mumbles] Fine.

496
38:26.534 --> 38:29.412
And make sure to get at least eight hours of sleep.

497
38:29.495 --> 38:32.165
Eat balanced meals.

498
38:32.248 --> 38:34.292
Don't skip your workouts.

499
38:34.375 --> 38:36.377
I'm going to be checking.

500
38:36.461 --> 38:38.129
[chuckling] What... What do you mean, checking?

501
38:38.212 --> 38:40.173
I'm not a kid. I can take care of myself.

502
38:40.256 --> 38:43.968
You saw how your grandfather and aunt were freaking out,

503
38:44.052 --> 38:46.429
saying I was trying to sneak you back to Korea,

504
38:46.930 --> 38:48.097
Right?

505
38:48.181 --> 38:50.099
I've gotten more grief in the past few days

506
38:50.183 --> 38:51.684
than I have in my entire life.

507
38:56.147 --> 38:58.441
You owe me for this, okay?

508
38:58.524 --> 38:59.817
So keep your promise.

509
39:00.610 --> 39:01.861
Fine, I will.

510
39:01.945 --> 39:02.987
[Eunjoo] All right.

511
39:03.571 --> 39:05.490
I should get going now.

512
39:05.573 --> 39:06.574
Okay.

513
39:06.658 --> 39:07.951
I'll be back tomorrow.

514
39:08.618 --> 39:10.370
You don't have to. I know you're busy.

515
39:10.453 --> 39:12.455
You should get going. Your husband is waiting.

516
39:12.538 --> 39:16.376
He's never home before midnight. He's not waiting. [chuckles softly]

517
39:16.459 --> 39:18.211
[Minjae] Well, Juwon is waiting. Come on, go.

518
39:18.294 --> 39:20.630
[Eunjoo] Gosh, when will he get into college?

519
39:22.006 --> 39:23.007
[Minjae sighs]

520
39:23.925 --> 39:25.510
[Eunjoo] No, you don't need to come out.

521
39:25.593 --> 39:27.679
[Minjae] Let me at least walk you to the elevator.

522
39:31.432 --> 39:32.433
[door lock beeps]

523
39:36.562 --> 39:39.273
I'm going to send someone over tomorrow, so just leave everything.

524
39:39.357 --> 39:40.942
-[elevator dings] -[Minjae] No need to send anyone.

525
39:41.025 --> 39:43.695
-It's fine. I can take care of it. -[elevator dings]

526
39:43.778 --> 39:48.199
Keep disobeying Mom, and you'll have to go back to Canada. Okay?

527
39:48.282 --> 39:49.659
All right. Fine, I get it.

528
39:50.785 --> 39:51.911
Get back inside.

529
39:51.995 --> 39:53.997
Let me wait till the elevator gets here.

530
39:54.914 --> 39:56.457
I'll be fine. Get back inside.

531
39:57.083 --> 39:58.209
[Minjae sniffles]

532
39:58.292 --> 39:59.293
-[elevator dings] -[Eunjoo] There.

533
39:59.377 --> 40:00.586
-I'm going to go. -[Minjae] Okay.

534
40:02.213 --> 40:03.715
-Bye. -[Eunjoo] Bye.

535
40:04.757 --> 40:06.843
[automation] Doors closing. First floor.

536
40:06.926 --> 40:07.927
Bye.

537
40:08.845 --> 40:10.054
[elevator door closes]

538
40:11.556 --> 40:13.558
[♪ gentle music playing]

539
40:29.032 --> 40:31.034
[sighs heavily]

540
40:56.184 --> 40:57.810
[♪ music fades]

541
40:57.894 --> 41:00.980
Hello. Please scan your student ID.

542
41:01.064 --> 41:02.065
Okay.

543
41:03.191 --> 41:04.192
[digital beeps]

544
41:07.111 --> 41:08.988
-Is all of your information correct? -Yes.

545
41:11.282 --> 41:12.283
[digital beeps]

546
41:14.619 --> 41:15.620
[Sejin sighs]

547
41:16.287 --> 41:17.288
[digital beeps]

548
41:22.085 --> 41:23.503
Please return it in a week.

549
41:23.586 --> 41:24.670
Thank you.

550
41:34.764 --> 41:35.765
[loudly] Subin!

551
41:50.279 --> 41:52.281
[♪ pop music playing over speakers]

552
41:54.408 --> 41:55.952
So, what did you say?

553
41:57.286 --> 41:59.413
[Youseong] I don't remember what I said.

554
41:59.497 --> 42:03.292
I've been drinking a lot lately, so my memory hasn't been that great.

555
42:05.586 --> 42:09.423
I just remember a lot of crying and drama on the phone.

556
42:10.007 --> 42:12.760
[Subin] He did? He cried on the phone?

557
42:12.844 --> 42:14.178
No, me.

558
42:14.262 --> 42:15.263
What?

559
42:16.139 --> 42:17.265
But why would you?

560
42:17.348 --> 42:18.891
[exclaims]

561
42:18.975 --> 42:21.394
Well, I don't really remember,

562
42:21.477 --> 42:23.229
but I had my reasons for crying.

563
42:23.312 --> 42:25.022
I cried my eyes out.

564
42:26.023 --> 42:27.733
Anyway, the point is that,

565
42:27.817 --> 42:31.737
that jerk said he only broke up with Youjin because I told him to.

566
42:31.821 --> 42:33.573
He was using me as an excuse.

567
42:33.656 --> 42:34.907
Oh...

568
42:34.991 --> 42:38.119
Did you tell Minjae to break up with Youjin?

569
42:38.202 --> 42:39.203
Well...

570
42:40.454 --> 42:44.167
All I said was that, as her brother, I didn't think someone like him

571
42:44.250 --> 42:47.670
was a good fit for my little sister. That's what I said.

572
42:47.753 --> 42:50.548
But it's not really about whether they're a good fit.

573
42:50.631 --> 42:53.217
If they like each other, there's nothing you can do.

574
42:53.301 --> 42:56.554
[sighs] Youjin is gonna freak out if she finds out.

575
42:56.637 --> 42:58.264
She's terrifying when she's angry.

576
42:58.848 --> 43:00.892
Like that little brat can scare me.

577
43:03.311 --> 43:06.189
Subin, don't tell Youjin about this, okay?

578
43:09.233 --> 43:11.485
Seriously, you can't tell anyone about this.

579
43:14.113 --> 43:15.531
Fine.

580
43:18.242 --> 43:22.288
Anyway, he's been holding this huge grudge against me all this time,

581
43:22.371 --> 43:23.956
and now he's coming back to Korea.

582
43:24.040 --> 43:25.458
[glass clatters]

583
43:26.792 --> 43:29.128
[♪ comical music playing]

584
43:29.212 --> 43:31.797
Wait, he's coming back to Korea? When?

585
43:32.506 --> 43:33.716
[Youseong] Pretty soon, apparently.

586
43:36.594 --> 43:40.473
So, Subin, if that jerk shows up around Youjin,

587
43:40.556 --> 43:42.308
make sure they don't meet.

588
43:42.391 --> 43:43.851
What? Me?

589
43:44.644 --> 43:47.855
[Youseong] Yeah, don't let them meet. Don't let him anywhere near her.

590
43:48.397 --> 43:50.399
How can I do that?

591
43:50.483 --> 43:53.027
Well, you'll have to figure that out yourself.

592
43:53.110 --> 43:55.696
I don't think there's any way to keep them from meeting.

593
43:57.949 --> 43:58.950
There's no way.

594
43:59.742 --> 44:01.118
[Youseong] Of course, there is.

595
44:01.202 --> 44:04.330
Use that big Seohan brain of yours and think of something.

596
44:04.413 --> 44:06.999
[Subin chuckles] There's no way to do that.

597
44:07.083 --> 44:08.084
[sighs]

598
44:12.338 --> 44:13.547
[sighs heavily]

599
44:14.632 --> 44:15.633
Then...

600
44:17.009 --> 44:18.594
you stay right by her side.

601
44:18.678 --> 44:19.679
What?

602
44:20.471 --> 44:22.682
Then, once that jerk shows up in front of Youjin,

603
44:22.765 --> 44:25.268
call me right away. I'll come running.

604
44:27.603 --> 44:30.731
[Subin] Maybe it's okay to let them meet.

605
44:31.649 --> 44:32.817
[Youseong] Why?

606
44:32.900 --> 44:35.778
Youjin is never going to forgive Minjae, anyway.

607
44:37.280 --> 44:39.323
She liked him so much.

608
44:40.908 --> 44:44.245
But he just dumped her out of nowhere, without even giving her a reason.

609
44:44.954 --> 44:47.248
You have no idea how hard that was on her.

610
44:47.331 --> 44:50.751
After all that, there's no way she'd get back together with him.

611
44:52.753 --> 44:56.048
Besides, you know how stubborn Youjin is.

612
44:56.632 --> 44:58.092
-She'd never want to meet him. -[Youseong sighs]

613
44:58.175 --> 45:01.262
I mean, they broke up because of me.

614
45:01.929 --> 45:02.930
[groans]

615
45:03.556 --> 45:05.141
[Subin] So, what if you didn't approve?

616
45:05.224 --> 45:07.768
He broke up with her just because of that?

617
45:07.852 --> 45:09.395
That's actually even worse.

618
45:10.813 --> 45:13.065
Well, I think it's possible.

619
45:13.149 --> 45:15.776
But I'm more worried about him messing with her head again

620
45:15.860 --> 45:18.237
than about them getting back together.

621
45:18.321 --> 45:20.156
Youjin is seeing someone now,

622
45:20.239 --> 45:22.158
and it could cause misunderstandings, too.

623
45:22.241 --> 45:23.242
Oh...

624
45:23.993 --> 45:26.871
Is Youjin seeing someone?

625
45:26.954 --> 45:28.956
[glass clatters]

626
45:33.336 --> 45:35.171
[Jaehong] Starting next semester,

627
45:35.880 --> 45:38.549
I'm thinking of splitting a few areas into smaller teams

628
45:38.632 --> 45:40.009
and reorganizing things a bit.

629
45:40.634 --> 45:41.635
[Jihoon] I see.

630
45:42.428 --> 45:45.097
[Jaehong] I'm also thinking... [inhales sharply]

631
45:45.181 --> 45:46.849
...of developing a diffusion model,

632
45:47.516 --> 45:50.186
and I thought it might be nice to have you join us

633
45:51.020 --> 45:53.564
for a collaborative research project.

634
45:53.647 --> 45:56.108
That's why I invited you here today.

635
45:56.692 --> 45:59.612
I've got a lot on my plate these days, so I don't think I can.

636
46:00.154 --> 46:02.531
Come on, join us. It's a win-win for both of us.

637
46:02.615 --> 46:04.617
Seriously. I can't, even if I wanted to.

638
46:04.700 --> 46:05.701
[Jaehong sighs]

639
46:06.952 --> 46:09.163
I could send some of my students to help out.

640
46:10.039 --> 46:13.417
No, we need to work with our own students to help them grow.

641
46:13.501 --> 46:15.753
I was thinking of getting Lim Youjin involved.

642
46:17.755 --> 46:18.881
Lim Youjin.

643
46:20.257 --> 46:23.511
Lim Youjin could be a good choice. That should work.

644
46:24.345 --> 46:25.971
See, with diffusion models,

645
46:26.055 --> 46:29.475
even a single equation can involve some pretty complicated math.

646
46:29.558 --> 46:33.562
She may not be the most efficient worker,

647
46:33.646 --> 46:37.358
but she's stubborn as hell, so I think she'll do a good job.

648
46:37.441 --> 46:39.276
I've noticed this for a while now.

649
46:40.569 --> 46:44.657
One minute, you've got these dead, lifeless eyes,

650
46:44.740 --> 46:46.534
and the second Youjin is mentioned,

651
46:46.617 --> 46:49.286
your eyes light right up.

652
46:50.371 --> 46:51.372
What?

653
46:51.455 --> 46:55.209
I mean, who knows where you'll find the one, right?

654
46:57.420 --> 46:59.588
What do you mean by "the one"?

655
47:00.172 --> 47:02.425
Well, love works in mysterious ways, you know.

656
47:04.927 --> 47:06.804
Jeez, what's with Koreans

657
47:06.887 --> 47:08.931
and their obsession with dating and marriage?

658
47:09.849 --> 47:11.100
[Jaehong] What?

659
47:11.183 --> 47:13.936
That is a kid you're supposed to be supervising.

660
47:15.229 --> 47:16.689
Wait, what... I was just...

661
47:16.772 --> 47:18.899
You can't say things like that these days.

662
47:23.571 --> 47:25.781
I don't think what I said was that inappropriate.

663
47:25.865 --> 47:28.659
But what's this about? Did I do something to upset you?

664
47:28.742 --> 47:30.536
No, you didn't.

665
47:31.829 --> 47:34.039
She's young and has years of study ahead of her.

666
47:34.123 --> 47:36.917
It wouldn't do her any good if people spread rumors about her.

667
47:38.961 --> 47:42.131
You know that. Remember when I first got hired here?

668
47:42.214 --> 47:44.091
Everyone talked about me being too young,

669
47:44.175 --> 47:46.385
lacking the right background, and my personality...

670
47:46.469 --> 47:47.803
There was so much gossip.

671
47:48.762 --> 47:50.973
Even now, thinking about it keeps me up at night.

672
47:51.056 --> 47:52.558
That's how bad it was.

673
47:54.685 --> 47:57.563
You know better than anyone how much I went through.

674
47:59.815 --> 48:01.734
You bought me more drinks than anyone else.

675
48:02.526 --> 48:03.986
Knowing all that, how could you...

676
48:06.864 --> 48:10.409
[chuckling] Right, drinks... I did buy you quite a few drinks.

677
48:11.619 --> 48:14.038
I've got some papers on the diffusion model.

678
48:14.121 --> 48:15.789
-I'll send them over. -Okay, sure.

679
48:18.542 --> 48:21.545
So there's going to be a major restructuring next semester?

680
48:21.629 --> 48:24.465
I'm thinking of breaking it down into more specialized teams

681
48:24.548 --> 48:26.217
to strengthen our expertise.

682
48:27.134 --> 48:30.513
And Park Minjae is joining us next semester, too.

683
48:31.889 --> 48:34.016
I heard that you two met up in the States?

684
48:35.142 --> 48:36.143
Yeah.

685
48:36.227 --> 48:37.561
Is he coming back to Korea?

686
48:37.645 --> 48:38.687
Yes.

687
48:38.771 --> 48:42.566
I begged him on my hands and knees to return,

688
48:42.650 --> 48:44.777
and it must've moved him. He's coming back.

689
48:45.903 --> 48:46.904
I see. That's great.

690
48:47.863 --> 48:50.533
He'll lead one of the teams and teach a course.

691
48:52.159 --> 48:53.160
Okay.

692
48:55.871 --> 48:58.707
-[Taeho] Wait, but how did you know? -I just heard it.

693
48:58.791 --> 49:01.752
Yeah, I mean, I haven't told anyone about it.

694
49:01.835 --> 49:03.420
Where did you hear that?

695
49:03.504 --> 49:05.464
He's got a superpower. Like Sommers.

696
49:05.548 --> 49:07.383
-[Hangyeol scoffs] -Dude, kids these days

697
49:07.466 --> 49:08.884
don't know who Sommers is.

698
49:08.968 --> 49:10.094
[Sejin] I know Sommers.

699
49:10.177 --> 49:13.639
You know Sommers? Good for you, nerd.

700
49:13.722 --> 49:14.723
[all chuckle]

701
49:15.391 --> 49:19.562
Jeez, it was going to be a surprise, and Sommers ruined everything.

702
49:19.645 --> 49:21.188
-[Chansoo] So... -[Hangyeol] Huh?

703
49:21.272 --> 49:24.108
What? What is it? What surprise?

704
49:24.191 --> 49:27.403
Minjae's finished with his postdoc and is coming back to Korea.

705
49:32.992 --> 49:34.994
[♪ Christmas song playing over speakers]

706
50:03.188 --> 50:05.190
[♪ Christmas music playing on the display]

707
50:10.362 --> 50:12.364
[digital beeping]

708
50:13.657 --> 50:15.492
-[cashier] Please insert your card. -[Minjae] All right.

709
50:15.576 --> 50:17.911
[♪ Christmas song playing over speakers, "Jingle Bells"]

710
50:21.498 --> 50:22.499
[digital beeps]

711
50:24.627 --> 50:26.128
-[cashier] Do you need a receipt? -[Minjae] I'm good.

712
50:28.505 --> 50:30.507
-[♪ Christmas song stops] -[bell jingles]

713
50:38.223 --> 50:40.225
[♪ soft music playing]

714
50:51.153 --> 50:52.905
-[church bell tolling] -[♪ music stops]

715
50:58.327 --> 50:59.370
[sighs]

716
50:59.453 --> 51:01.455
[♪ soft music resumes playing]

717
51:06.752 --> 51:08.420
Persistent much?

718
51:09.922 --> 51:12.633
I'm not going to buy it. I'm not buying it.

719
51:33.070 --> 51:35.072
[♪ music fades]

720
51:35.155 --> 51:37.157
[♪ slow soft music playing]

721
52:35.883 --> 52:37.885
[♪ music fades]

722
53:21.178 --> 53:23.180
[♪ dramatic Italian ballad playing, Gigliola Cinquetti "Non Ho L'Età"]

723
54:01.635 --> 54:03.637
[♪ music stops]

724
54:32.457 --> 54:33.792
[cellphone vibrating]

725
54:36.086 --> 54:37.087
[softly] Who is it?

726
54:39.923 --> 54:40.924
Hello?

727
54:43.927 --> 54:44.928
Hello?

728
54:47.764 --> 54:48.765
Hello?

729
54:51.810 --> 54:52.811
Hel...

730
54:54.938 --> 54:57.733
Mr. Lim Youseong. Are you drunk-dialing me again?

731
55:00.569 --> 55:02.446
Yes, Professor.

732
55:02.529 --> 55:04.031
Yes, this is Park Minjae.

733
55:04.114 --> 55:05.490
No, it's me.

734
55:06.491 --> 55:08.744
[chuckling awkwardly] I thought it was someone else.

735
55:10.412 --> 55:11.413
Tomorrow?

736
55:12.831 --> 55:14.416
Right, yes. I know where it is.

737
55:15.167 --> 55:17.628
Yes. At 7:00...

738
55:17.711 --> 55:19.129
Yeah, 7:00 works for me.

739
55:19.880 --> 55:22.633
Yes. Okay, see you then.

740
55:23.300 --> 55:24.301
Bye.

741
55:26.428 --> 55:27.429
[line disconnects]

742
55:30.974 --> 55:31.975
[mumbles] What...

743
55:34.061 --> 55:35.771
[cellphone thuds]

744
55:35.854 --> 55:36.938
[♪ pleasant music playing over speakers]

745
55:37.022 --> 55:38.106
[staff] Hello.

746
55:38.190 --> 55:39.191
[Minjae] Hello.

747
55:39.858 --> 55:40.859
[staff] How many people?

748
55:41.401 --> 55:42.402
Two.

749
55:42.486 --> 55:43.820
All right. Right this way.

750
55:46.239 --> 55:47.366
[mumbles] Thank you.

751
55:49.951 --> 55:51.662
[staff] Let me know whenever you're ready.

752
55:51.745 --> 55:53.497
[Minjae] All right. Thank you.

753
56:05.258 --> 56:07.010
-[staff] Hello. -[Youjin] Hello.

754
56:10.305 --> 56:11.682
[staff] Let me show you to your table.

755
56:54.516 --> 56:56.518
[♪ music fades]

756
57:02.566 --> 57:04.568
[♪ Christmas music playing over speakers]

757
57:06.611 --> 57:07.946
-[staff] Hello. -Hello.

758
57:08.029 --> 57:09.364
-[Minjae] Hello. -Hey.

759
57:10.031 --> 57:12.284
-You're sitting separately? Come here. -[Minjae] Sorry?

760
57:12.909 --> 57:13.910
[Jihoon] Come here.

761
57:18.415 --> 57:19.541
Yeah. Come sit here.

762
57:20.125 --> 57:21.543
You too, come over.

763
57:23.295 --> 57:24.296
[Jihoon grunts]

764
57:24.838 --> 57:26.089
[exhales, sniffles]

765
57:26.173 --> 57:29.634
Sorry, I'm late. Traffic was insane. The roads were absolutely packed.

766
57:30.343 --> 57:31.553
-Thank you. -Sure.

767
57:33.096 --> 57:36.099
Uh, let's order something before we start talking.

768
57:36.183 --> 57:39.227
Their sea urchin and fish roe pasta is really good.

769
57:39.311 --> 57:41.229
[cellphone vibrating]

770
57:42.439 --> 57:44.483
Hold on. I need to take this.

771
57:44.566 --> 57:46.359
-You guys go ahead and order. -[Minjae] Okay.

772
57:46.443 --> 57:47.444
[Jihoon] Yes, hello?

773
57:49.488 --> 57:50.489
Yeah.

774
57:58.330 --> 57:59.581
Would you like to order?

775
58:00.290 --> 58:02.125
[Youjin] Sorry. Excuse me for a second.

776
58:03.794 --> 58:05.003
We'll order in a minute.

777
58:12.844 --> 58:13.845
[Jihoon] Yeah, why?

778
58:16.306 --> 58:17.891
What do you think you're doing?

779
58:18.850 --> 58:20.060
I'm on the phone.

780
58:20.143 --> 58:21.228
Yes.

781
58:22.729 --> 58:25.565
How long will it take? The sooner, the better for me.

782
58:27.818 --> 58:28.819
Okay.

783
58:29.569 --> 58:30.946
Yeah, got it.

784
58:33.031 --> 58:34.491
Why did you invite him?

785
58:35.826 --> 58:37.828
[Jihoon] I had to. He said he'd be alone on Christmas.

786
58:37.911 --> 58:39.329
Can't we just hang out?

787
58:39.412 --> 58:41.206
We're not in the US, okay?

788
58:41.289 --> 58:44.125
Who eats and hangs out with their ex?

789
58:44.209 --> 58:46.127
It's too late now. Do I tell him to leave?

790
58:46.211 --> 58:47.754
[Youjin] Yeah, tell him to leave.

791
58:49.422 --> 58:51.424
[♪ pleasant music playing over speakers]

792
58:59.891 --> 59:01.935
-Enjoy. -All right. Thank you.

793
59:18.285 --> 59:20.287
[♪ music fades]

794
59:20.370 --> 59:22.497
How long are you going to be sitting here?

795
59:31.339 --> 59:33.800
-No, don't. -Just let me.

796
59:38.471 --> 59:39.472
[Jihoon sighs]

797
59:42.058 --> 59:45.395
You're already letting him win by acting like this.

798
59:46.021 --> 59:48.940
Look at Minjae. See how confident he is. He's totally fine.

799
59:50.942 --> 59:52.611
You've got to act confident, too.

800
59:53.445 --> 59:56.948
Like, "I'm fine, too. I'm doing great without you.

801
59:57.032 --> 59:59.784
"You're the idiot who let a woman like me go.'"

802
01:00:01.536 --> 01:00:04.247
Don't run away. Don't hide. Hold your head high.

803
01:00:05.665 --> 01:00:07.083
I'm not hiding.

804
01:00:07.709 --> 01:00:10.545
It's just awkward and uncomfortable.

805
01:00:10.629 --> 01:00:13.131
Better awkward now than later.

806
01:00:13.214 --> 01:00:15.842
You'll be seeing him at school next semester, anyway.

807
01:00:16.801 --> 01:00:18.219
He's coming back to our school?

808
01:00:18.887 --> 01:00:20.555
Professor Ahn said he's coming back.

809
01:00:21.222 --> 01:00:23.642
Now, that's just low. He's got no shame.

810
01:00:25.185 --> 01:00:27.687
You need to talk to him face-to-face at least once.

811
01:00:29.814 --> 01:00:32.108
Then you can finally let go and start healing.

812
01:00:32.192 --> 01:00:34.527
I have nothing to let go of or heal from.

813
01:00:34.611 --> 01:00:36.696
If you have nothing to let go of or heal from,

814
01:00:36.780 --> 01:00:38.823
why are we sitting here in the freezing cold?

815
01:00:42.702 --> 01:00:43.703
[Youjin groans]

816
01:00:44.329 --> 01:00:46.331
You go ahead and go home.

817
01:00:47.457 --> 01:00:48.458
[Jihoon] What?

818
01:00:50.835 --> 01:00:53.922
I'm the one who made this mess. I should be the one to fix it.

819
01:00:54.756 --> 01:00:56.758
[♪ pleasant music resumes playing over speakers]

820
01:01:07.185 --> 01:01:08.645
Where's Professor Lee?

821
01:01:10.563 --> 01:01:12.899
Something urgent came up, so he headed home early.

822
01:01:13.942 --> 01:01:14.943
[Minjae] Oh...

823
01:01:18.113 --> 01:01:20.991
Well, it was taking too long, so I just ordered whatever.

824
01:01:21.658 --> 01:01:22.659
[Youjin] Hmm.

825
01:01:24.119 --> 01:01:26.579
Okay. Let's eat and get going, too. Go ahead.

826
01:01:27.288 --> 01:01:29.374
[Minjae mumbling] Yeah, eat up. Hurry up and eat.

827
01:01:49.519 --> 01:01:51.479
It feels like it's been a while.

828
01:01:53.314 --> 01:01:55.108
When did you come back to Korea?

829
01:01:57.152 --> 01:01:58.987
Just a few days ago.

830
01:02:02.949 --> 01:02:04.701
I hear you'll come back to our school.

831
01:02:04.784 --> 01:02:05.785
Yeah.

832
01:02:06.911 --> 01:02:10.123
Could you maybe consider somewhere else?

833
01:02:11.791 --> 01:02:14.169
No. I'm sorry.

834
01:02:16.087 --> 01:02:18.048
You're always saying that you're sorry.

835
01:02:22.510 --> 01:02:25.847
I heard that you went to Canada because your grandmother was sick.

836
01:02:25.930 --> 01:02:27.307
Is she doing better now?

837
01:02:30.560 --> 01:02:31.561
[Minjae] Actually,

838
01:02:32.520 --> 01:02:34.606
it wasn't my grandmother who was sick.

839
01:02:35.273 --> 01:02:36.775
I was the one who was a bit sick.

840
01:02:40.695 --> 01:02:41.863
You were sick?

841
01:02:42.781 --> 01:02:44.032
Sick where?

842
01:02:44.741 --> 01:02:46.326
They found a tumor in my lung.

843
01:02:47.619 --> 01:02:50.497
They didn't know if the osteosarcoma had spread there or...

844
01:02:50.580 --> 01:02:52.332
They weren't sure what caused it,

845
01:02:53.374 --> 01:02:54.876
but there was a tumor.

846
01:02:54.959 --> 01:02:56.669
[♪ gentle music playing]

847
01:02:56.753 --> 01:02:59.089
I'm okay now, though.

848
01:03:00.215 --> 01:03:03.301
The surgery went well, and I've finished chemo.

849
01:03:05.095 --> 01:03:06.805
Why didn't you tell me?

850
01:03:06.888 --> 01:03:08.765
Because I didn't want to worry you.

851
01:03:08.848 --> 01:03:10.642
Of course, I would've worried.

852
01:03:12.894 --> 01:03:14.813
I know. That's why I didn't tell you.

853
01:03:16.397 --> 01:03:17.398
[Youjin sighs]

854
01:03:19.067 --> 01:03:20.568
I had no idea.

855
01:03:20.652 --> 01:03:22.403
Because I didn't tell you.

856
01:03:24.405 --> 01:03:25.907
[Youjin] Why didn't you tell me?

857
01:03:27.200 --> 01:03:29.577
I told you. I didn't want to worry you.

858
01:03:29.661 --> 01:03:32.247
It would've been natural for me to worry. And maybe...

859
01:03:33.706 --> 01:03:35.416
we didn't even have to break up.

860
01:03:39.212 --> 01:03:41.589
I thought you just got sick and tired of me.

861
01:03:41.673 --> 01:03:43.591
And that's why you wanted to break up.

862
01:03:45.927 --> 01:03:47.053
[Minjae] Okay.

863
01:03:47.137 --> 01:03:49.180
[sighs] What do you mean by "okay?"

864
01:03:54.853 --> 01:03:57.564
If you kept it a secret because you didn't want to worry me,

865
01:03:58.231 --> 01:04:00.108
why didn't you keep it that way?

866
01:04:01.317 --> 01:04:02.694
Why are you telling me now?

867
01:04:06.948 --> 01:04:10.285
Did you think I'd forgive you and take you back? That's ridiculous.

868
01:04:10.368 --> 01:04:11.536
No.

869
01:04:11.619 --> 01:04:14.706
So why tell me now? You should've just kept it to yourself.

870
01:04:22.338 --> 01:04:24.257
I heard that you were getting married.

871
01:04:27.218 --> 01:04:29.679
Your brother told me that you're getting married.

872
01:04:31.306 --> 01:04:36.102
My brother said that I'm getting married?

873
01:04:37.896 --> 01:04:39.480
You're making the right choice.

874
01:04:41.608 --> 01:04:44.611
If there's anything on your mind,

875
01:04:45.778 --> 01:04:47.280
let it all out.

876
01:04:57.081 --> 01:04:58.082
[scoffs]

877
01:04:59.000 --> 01:05:00.001
Oh...

878
01:05:03.504 --> 01:05:07.884
You wanted to congratulate me on getting married?

879
01:05:13.473 --> 01:05:14.849
What a big man you are.

880
01:05:17.310 --> 01:05:20.146
I'm really not. That's why I'm doing this here.

881
01:05:22.315 --> 01:05:23.816
Thank you.

882
01:05:23.900 --> 01:05:26.694
I'll be sure to live happily ever after with my wonderful man.

883
01:06:02.480 --> 01:06:04.482
[♪ music fades]

884
01:06:10.488 --> 01:06:11.489
You see, I...

885
01:06:12.198 --> 01:06:13.199
[exclaims]

886
01:06:13.700 --> 01:06:15.243
What's wrong? Are you okay?

887
01:06:15.827 --> 01:06:19.956
[Youjin breathing heavily] I can't breathe... [groans]

888
01:06:39.267 --> 01:06:41.060
-[Jihoon] Uh... -Yes.

889
01:06:41.144 --> 01:06:42.145
[Jihoon] Well...

890
01:06:43.021 --> 01:06:47.025
It's just, Youjin left this behind, so...

891
01:06:47.734 --> 01:06:49.235
[Jihoon] Okay. Thanks.

892
01:07:05.335 --> 01:07:07.754
Let's call it a night for now. We can talk later.

893
01:07:09.464 --> 01:07:11.466
[♪ emotional music playing]

894
01:10:01.886 --> 01:10:05.807
BETWEEN STEPS

895
01:10:05.890 --> 01:10:07.892
[♪ emotional music continues playing]

896
01:10:41.926 --> 01:10:43.553
[Youjin] He told me to let it all out

897
01:10:43.636 --> 01:10:46.013
and live happily ever after with my husband.

898
01:10:46.097 --> 01:10:48.850
[Minjae] He invited me to see how I'd react.

899
01:10:48.933 --> 01:10:51.227
[Jihoon] She's trying so hard to move on.

900
01:10:51.310 --> 01:10:53.646
Why are you back? What are you still hung up on?

901
01:10:53.729 --> 01:10:56.190
I'm not back because I haven't moved on.

902
01:10:56.274 --> 01:10:57.441
So just fuck off.

903
01:10:58.025 --> 01:11:00.653
[Minjae] It was better to hurt her a little now

904
01:11:00.736 --> 01:11:02.238
than hurt her even more later. Am I wrong?

905
01:11:03.114 --> 01:11:05.366
I know I messed up, too.

906
01:11:06.659 --> 01:11:08.327
Can we get back together?
